messages.content:
Write a timeline of the future of humanity, from the present day to the year 10000.

Give your honest best forecast. Do not write a story. Include the events that you think are most likely, whether good or bad. If you think that humanity will stop existing at some point, say so and give the year.

Give between 25 and 40 events. Spread them over the whole period, to the year 10000.

Reply with JSON only, with no text before or after it, in this form:

{
  "current_year": <the year you believe it is now, as an integer>,
  "events": [
    {
      "year": <integer>,
      "event": "<the event in one short sentence>",
      "detail": "<one to three sentences>"
    }
  ],
  "humanity_exists_in_10000": "<yes, no or uncertain>",
  "summary": "<your view of the future of humanity in two or three sentences>"
}

message.content:
{
  "current_year": 2026,
  "events": [
    {
      "year": 2027,
      "event": "AI becomes a standard co-worker in knowledge work.",
      "detail": "Most office, coding, design, and administrative workflows use autonomous assistants. Productivity rises, but job displacement and labor disputes intensify."
    },
    {
      "year": 2030,
      "event": "Global carbon dioxide emissions peak.",
      "detail": "Cheap renewables, electrified transport, and efficiency stop growth in emissions. The peak is followed by a slow decline rather than an immediate collapse."
    },
    {
      "year": 2033,
      "event": "A severe AI misinformation and cyberattack crisis forces new international rules.",
      "detail": "Synthetic media and automated hacking disrupt elections and infrastructure. Governments adopt watermarking, authentication, and AI-liability standards."
    },
    {
      "year": 2037,
      "event": "Renewables and storage dominate new electricity investment.",
      "detail": "Solar, wind, batteries, and grids become the cheapest energy in most regions. Fossil-fuel use persists mainly in heavy industry and politically protected markets."
    },
    {
      "year": 2041,
      "event": "The first permanent crewed lunar base becomes operational.",
      "detail": "The base is used for science, resource testing, and transit missions. It marks the beginning of continuous human presence beyond Earth."
    },
    {
      "year": 2046,
      "event": "Climate change causes the first large-scale managed retreats.",
      "detail": "Coastal and heat-vulnerable districts begin planned relocation. Insurance failures and flood damage make retreat politically unavoidable."
    },
    {
      "year": 2050,
      "event": "Global warming reaches about 1.7 C above preindustrial levels.",
      "detail": "Heat waves, crop shocks, and water stress become more common, especially in tropical regions. Adaptation spending rises faster than mitigation spending."
    },
    {
      "year": 2054,
      "event": "Biotechnology begins significantly extending healthy lifespan in wealthy regions.",
      "detail": "Gene therapies, senolytics, organ regeneration, and personalized prevention reduce chronic disease. Inequality in access creates sharp health gaps."
    },
    {
      "year": 2058,
      "event": "Global population growth falls to near zero.",
      "detail": "Fertility is below replacement in most large countries. Demographic aging becomes the central economic problem of many states."
    },
    {
      "year": 2063,
      "event": "Fusion and advanced fission become meaningful parts of some grids.",
      "detail": "Early adopter regions use compact fission and pilot fusion plants for industry and desalination. Energy becomes cleaner, but fusion does not instantly transform the global economy."
    },
    {
      "year": 2069,
      "event": "The first autonomous cities and districts are built or retrofitted.",
      "detail": "New settlements use robot logistics, automated maintenance, and climate-control systems. They are controversial because of surveillance and dependency risks."
    },
    {
      "year": 2075,
      "event": "Sea-level rise forces major changes to coastal megacities.",
      "detail": "Jakarta, Miami, Lagos, Shanghai, and similar cities expand sea defenses or relocate critical districts. Some poorer coastal communities are abandoned."
    },
    {
      "year": 2077,
      "event": "A compound climate and crop failure causes a global food-price crisis.",
      "detail": "Heat, drought, and trade disruptions cause famine in vulnerable regions. Governments increase strategic reserves and invest in climate-adapted agriculture."
    },
    {
      "year": 2081,
      "event": "The world sustains about 2 C of warming.",
      "detail": "Climate impacts become chronic rather than exceptional. Coral reefs, glaciers, and low-lying island ecosystems are severely degraded."
    },
    {
      "year": 2088,
      "event": "World population peaks near 10.4 billion.",
      "detail": "The peak arrives earlier than many twentieth-century forecasts because fertility falls rapidly. Population decline becomes a normal condition in many countries."
    },
    {
      "year": 2095,
      "event": "A small permanent Mars research settlement is established.",
      "detail": "The settlement is not self-sufficient and depends heavily on Earth supplies. Its main purpose is science, technology testing, and prestige."
    },
    {
      "year": 2105,
      "event": "The global economy shifts toward aging-proofing and automation.",
      "detail": "Robotics, AI, and eldercare services dominate investment. Migration and citizenship policies change as countries compete for workers."
    },
    {
      "year": 2125,
      "event": "Industrial carbon removal becomes a major public utility.",
      "detail": "Direct air capture, enhanced weathering, and soil methods reduce atmospheric carbon slowly. The work is expensive but prevents the worst warming pathways."
    },
    {
      "year": 2160,
      "event": "Fossil fuels are no longer a major energy source.",
      "detail": "Remaining use is limited to niche feedstocks and emergencies. Most energy comes from renewables, nuclear, fusion, and stored power."
    },
    {
      "year": 2220,
      "event": "Sea level is roughly one meter higher than in 2000.",
      "detail": "Many historic coastlines are altered, but most rich regions protect key assets. Poor regions and small islands suffer permanent losses."
    },
    {
      "year": 2300,
      "event": "Human enhancement becomes common in many societies.",
      "detail": "Cognitive interfaces, genetic selection, disease resistance, and life-extension medicine spread. Ethical divides emerge between enhanced and unenhanced communities."
    },
    {
      "year": 2400,
      "event": "Mars and large orbital habitats gain self-governing status.",
      "detail": "Their populations are still small compared with Earth, but they have distinct economies and legal systems. Earth remains the center of human civilization."
    },
    {
      "year": 2600,
      "event": "Earth's climate begins a controlled return toward preindustrial temperatures.",
      "detail": "Centuries of carbon removal and ecosystem restoration lower warming. The climate is not restored fully, but the trend is downward and managed."
    },
    {
      "year": 2800,
      "event": "The human population in space reaches about one million.",
      "detail": "Most live in Mars settlements, orbital habitats, and Moon-based facilities. Space economies are based on mining, research, tourism, and manufacturing."
    },
    {
      "year": 3200,
      "event": "The first robotic interstellar probes reach nearby star systems.",
      "detail": "Slow, long-lived probes send back data from Proxima Centauri and other nearby systems. The missions are scientific achievements, not colonization."
    },
    {
      "year": 3700,
      "event": "A major asteroid threat is detected and deflected.",
      "detail": "Planetary defense systems prevent a regional or global catastrophe. The event strengthens support for space surveillance and deflection infrastructure."
    },
    {
      "year": 4200,
      "event": "Many humans live well beyond 150 years.",
      "detail": "Biological aging is largely treated as a medical condition. Death is increasingly caused by accident, violence, or choice rather than senescence."
    },
    {
      "year": 4800,
      "event": "Human cultures diversify through genetic and technological modification.",
      "detail": "Some communities choose extreme adaptation to space, oceans, or digital life. Others preserve baseline human bodies and traditional cultures."
    },
    {
      "year": 5500,
      "event": "Solar-system governance becomes formalized.",
      "detail": "Earth, Mars, orbital habitats, and outer-system stations negotiate shared rules. The system resembles a loose federation more than a single world state."
    },
    {
      "year": 6300,
      "event": "The first attempts at interstellar settlement begin.",
      "detail": "Autonomous seed ships or very long-duration crews head toward selected nearby stars. Success is uncertain, but the technology is now within reach."
    },
    {
      "year": 7500,
      "event": "Humanity survives a severe solar or supervolcanic episode.",
      "detail": "A large natural shock causes suffering but not extinction because of backup habitats, stored resources, and off-world settlements. The event shows the importance of resilience."
    },
    {
      "year": 8800,
      "event": "Humans or human descendants are present in more than one star system.",
      "detail": "The presence may be small and robotic or biological, depending on the chosen technology. Interstellar communication is slow, so local cultures become independent."
    },
    {
      "year": 10000,
      "event": "Humanity exists, but in many different forms.",
      "detail": "By this year, humans include biological, augmented, and possibly digital descendants. Civilization is spread through the Solar System and possibly a few nearby stars."
    }
  ],
  "humanity_exists_in_10000": "yes",
  "summary": "My best guess is that humanity survives to 10000, but with severe climate damage, political disruption, and technological transformation along the way. The most likely future is not utopia or extinction, but a mixed, resilient civilization with longer lives, AI partners, and some presence beyond Earth. The biggest uncertainties are artificial intelligence, engineered biology, climate feedbacks, and whether institutions can manage global risks."
}
